00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.611
The revelations are part of Dominion

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.612
Voting Systems

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.482
$1.6 billion lawsuit against Fox.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:16.349
And CNN's

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.917
Brian Todd is digging into the damning

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.052
testimony and messages.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.520
So tell us more, Brian.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.588
Pamela, these messages

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.623
reflect real angst and conflicts

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.524
within the top

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.960
echelons of Fox News right after the

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.928
2020 election as well.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.598
As a hefty dose of hypocrisy.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.034
Immediately after Joe

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.969
Biden's 2020 victory,

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:36.669
Fox News

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.971
hosts were unabashed

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.739
in promoting the false declarations

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.107
that the election had been stolen

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.008
from Donald Trump.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.610
Electronic voting machines

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.112
didn't allow people to vote, apparently,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.980
and that whatever

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.548
you think of it, the cause of it

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.583
it shakes people's faith in the system

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.019
that is an actual threat to democracy.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:56.156
It will be impossible to ever know

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.993
the true fair accurate election results.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.327
But tonight, a new court

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.063
filing shows that in private,

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.164
Fox host Tucker

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.533
Carlson, Laura Ingraham and Sean Hannity

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.068
were brutally ridiculing

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.569
the claims of election fraud

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.071
and the people who were making them

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.173
their private messages in a legal filing.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.008
That's part of Dominion Voting Systems.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.944
$1.6 billion lawsuit against Fox News

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.345
one person they insulted.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.347
Trump campaign lawyer Sidney Powell,

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.450
a vociferous election line promoter.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.885
What we are really dealing with here

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.987
and uncovering more by the day

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:31.724
is the massive influence

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.159
of communist money

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.395
in one text revealed in the court filing.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.830
Tucker Carlson texted

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.298
Laura Ingraham saying quote,

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.833
Sidney Powell is lying.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.533
I caught her.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.401
It's insane.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.869
Ingraham responded, quote,

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.337
Sidney is a complete nut.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.505
No one will work with her.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.639
Ditto with Rudy.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.141
A reference to Trump lawyer Rudy

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.410
Giuliani and his post-election claims

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.847
there was a plan from a centralized place

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.715
to execute

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.717
these various acts of voter fraud.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.785
In other messages,

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.386
Sean Hannity said Giuliani

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.455
was, quote, acting like an insane person.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.891
Ingram described Giuliani as an idiot.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.059
Fox Corp.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.260
Chairman Rupert Murdoch

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.962
We still have freedom of speech.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.429
Said it

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:09.929
was, quote,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.663
really bad

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.233
that Giuliani was advising Trump.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.535
They have one version of the world

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.070
that they keep to themselves.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.438
And another version of the world

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.306
that they broadcast to the viewers.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.342
The two are entirely incompatible.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.910
But Fox kept promoting

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.145
election denialism.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.247
Why the filings in the Dominion suit

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.882
illustrate that Fox executives

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:29.415
were worried

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.618
about losing viewers to Newsmax,

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.186
a smaller conservative channel

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.487
that was constantly pushing

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.455
election denial.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:35.788
Trump

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.857
himself furious that Fox had called

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.659
Arizona for Biden, Arizona.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.027
11 electoral votes

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.362
had encouraged his followers

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.664
to switch to Newsmax since 2002.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:45.331
Fox News

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.367
has basically been the preeminent

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:50.270
ratings champion in cable news.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:53.573
And you see here the moment that they see

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.541
any sign

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.177
that might be slipping away it's panic.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.478
But the Dominion filings

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.445
also say that

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.280
when then-President

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.514
Trump tried to call in

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.284
to Fox on January 6th,

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.585
the day his supporters attacked

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.253
the Capitol Fox executives

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.088
refused to put Trump on the air.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.191
Fox News has

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.258
denied Dominion's

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.560
claims in the lawsuit

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.662
says its proud of its 2020

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.696
election coverage

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.130
and says

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:17.630
these court

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.698
filings contained

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.167
Cherry-picked quotes lacking context.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.302
In a statement, Fox

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.970
accused Dominion of generating,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.738
quote, noise and confusion

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.973
and said The core of this case

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.808
remains to be about freedom of the press

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.843
and freedom of speech. Pamela.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.879
All right, Brian Todd, thanks so much.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:33.780
I want to bring in

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.882
CNN senior media reporter Oliver Darcy,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.516
along with Maggie

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:37.650
Haberman of The New York Times.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.586
She is also a CNN political analyst.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.553
So, Maggie,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.888
these court documents,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.457
they reveal a stunning level of hypocrisy

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.558
on the part of FOX.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.960
What does this reveal about

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.761
just how strong of a grip

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.430
the former president had on the network?

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.132
It's it's quite striking.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.901
And you saw this evolution over time.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:55.802
Rupert Murdoch had always

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.637
wanted to be close to a U.S. president.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.338
He got that

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.505
when Donald Trump was elected,

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.273
even though they really did

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.741
not have much of a relationship

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.875
to speak of Rupert Murdoch

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.410
and never thought very highly of him.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.412
But by the time he was in office,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.647
there was a synergy.

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:08.281
And Fox

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.950
clearly saw a benefit in terms of viewers

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.453
and ratings in staying close to Trump.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.821
What I was very struck

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.421
by, Pamela,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.323
was this claim in the suit

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.892
that Trump had tried to get on Lou Dobbs

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.395
after the riot had had taken place

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.330
